## Frequently asked questions

### Is AI recruiting software worth it for a small startup?

It can be, if it removes a real bottleneck, such as screening hundreds of applicants or running many first-round calls. Start with a free tier on one role and measure the time saved.

### Can AI recruiting software replace a recruiter?

No. It handles repetitive work like first-pass screening, drafting and scheduling. People still need to build relationships, judge fit and make decisions.

### Is AI candidate screening biased?

It can be, depending on how it's built. Look for tools that hide protected characteristics from the AI, explain their scores with evidence and keep humans responsible for decisions.

### What's the difference between an ATS and AI recruiting software?

An ATS tracks candidates through your hiring stages. AI recruiting software adds features like screening, ranking, drafting and interviewing. Many tools, including GetHired, now combine both.

### How do I know if an AI screening score is accurate?

Compare it with your own review of the same applicants on a real role, and check the evidence it gives. A good tool's reasons should hold up when you read the resume.

